# Linear board — state authority and blocking

## Context

SlugBase uses **Linear** (SlugBase team, issue key `SB-N`) as the **primary** tracker. GitHub Issues (`mdg-labs/slugbase`) are a **two-way synced mirror** for Development panel linking and `fixes #N` auto-close on `main`.

Two separate status systems:

| System | Authority | Who manages |
|---|---|---|
| **Linear workflow state** | Day-to-day tracking | Agents via Linear MCP `save_issue` (`state`) |
| **GitHub issue state** (`open`/`closed`) | Release | Commit body `fixes #N` on `main` only |

**Linear state is what matters** for orchestration, intake, and blocking. Verifiers set **Done** on Linear; the GitHub mirror often stays `open` until release to `main`.

## Blocking dependencies — unblocked when Linear state is Done or Closed

A task that depends on another issue (e.g. "Depends on: SB-325" / `#325`) is **unblocked** when the blocking issue's Linear state is **Done** or **Closed** — regardless of GitHub issue state alone.

| Linear state | GitHub issue state | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Done | `open` (typical) | Verified on `staging` — **unblocks dependents** |
| Closed | `closed` | Released on `main` — ceremonial; work was usable at Done |

**Corollary:** Never use GitHub `open`/`closed` alone to judge if a dependency is resolved. Check **Linear state**.

## Agent workflow

| Operation | Tool |
|---|---|
| Create / update issues | Linear MCP `save_issue` (team: `SlugBase`) |
| Set state (In Progress, Done, …) | Linear MCP `save_issue` (`state`) |
| Comments (verifier) | Linear `list_comments` + `save_comment` (`parentId` reply on GitHub-linked thread) |
| Read synced GitHub # | Linear `get_issue` links/attachments or MCP `user-github` `issue_read` |

Reference: `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/linear-board.md`

## Forbidden

- **GraphQL `updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue`** on GitHub Project 2 — agents no longer set GitHub Projects board Status.
- **`gh project item-list`**, **`addProjectV2ItemById`** — obsolete for agent workflow.
- **Setting GitHub issue state** (`open`/`closed`) directly — commit keywords on `main` only.
- **Issue keys in commit subjects** — `SB-N` and `#N` belong in commit **body** only (rule `07-issue-commit-linking.mdc`).

## Anti-patterns

```bash
# NEVER — GitHub project board status (deprecated)
gh api graphql -f 'query=mutation { updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue(...) }'

# NEVER — keys in commit subject
git commit -m "feat(auth)[SB-12][#612]: add sessions"

# CORRECT — Linear state + body-only keys
# save_issue: { id: "SB-12", state: "In Progress" }
git commit -m "feat(auth): add sessions

fixes SB-12
fixes #612"
```
